{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/UseHotkeyOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UseHotkeyOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"> = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options for the hotkey behavior"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkey } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst count = ref(0)\n\n// Callback always has access to latest count value\nuseHotkey('Mod+S', (event, { hotkey }) => {\n  console.log(`Save triggered, count is ${count.value}`)\n  handleSave()\n})\n</script>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkey } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst isOpen = ref(false)\n\n// enabled option is reactive\nuseHotkey('Escape', () => {\n  isOpen.value = false\n}, { enabled: isOpen })\n</script>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkey } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst editorRef = ref<HTMLDivElement | null>(null)\n\n// Scoped to a specific element\nuseHotkey('Mod+S', () => {\n  save()\n}, { target: editorRef })\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div ref=\"editorRef\">...</div>\n</template>","lang":"vue"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"hotkey","text":"hotkey","level":3},{"id":"callback","text":"callback","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useHotkey(\n   hotkey, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkey.ts:99](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHotkey.ts#L99)\n\nVue composable for registering a keyboard hotkey.\n\nUses the singleton HotkeyManager for efficient event handling.\nThe callback receives both the keyboard event and a context object\ncontaining the hotkey string and parsed hotkey.\n\nThis composable automatically tracks reactive dependencies and updates\nthe registration when options or the callback change.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### hotkey\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<`RegisterableHotkey`\\>\n\nThe hotkey string (e.g., 'Mod+S', 'Escape') or RawHotkey object (supports `mod` for cross-platform)\n\n### callback\n\n`HotkeyCallback`\n\nThe function to call when the hotkey is pressed\n\n### options?\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<[`UseHotkeyOptions`](../interfaces/UseHotkeyOptions.md)\\> = `{}`\n\nOptions for the hotkey behavior\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Examples\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkey } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst count = ref(0)\n\n// Callback always has access to latest count value\nuseHotkey('Mod+S', (event, { hotkey }) => {\n  console.log(`Save triggered, count is ${count.value}`)\n  handleSave()\n})\n</script>\n```\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkey } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst isOpen = ref(false)\n\n// enabled option is reactive\nuseHotkey('Escape', () => {\n  isOpen.value = false\n}, { enabled: isOpen })\n</script>\n```\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkey } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst editorRef = ref<HTMLDivElement | null>(null)\n\n// Scoped to a specific element\nuseHotkey('Mod+S', () => {\n  save()\n}, { target: editorRef })\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div ref=\"editorRef\">...</div>\n</template>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useHotkey\ntitle: useHotkey\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useHotkey(\n   hotkey, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkey.ts:99](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHotkey.ts#L99)\n\nVue composable for registering a keyboard hotkey.\n\nUses the singleton HotkeyManager for efficient event handling.\nThe callback receives both the keyboard event and a context object\ncontaining the hotkey string and parsed hotkey.\n\nThis composable automatically tracks reactive dependencies and updates\nthe registration when options or the callback change.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### hotkey\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<`RegisterableHotkey`\\>\n\nThe hotkey string (e.g., 'Mod+S', 'Escape') or RawHotkey object (supports `mod` for cross-platform)\n\n### callback\n\n`HotkeyCallback`\n\nThe function to call when the hotkey is pressed\n\n### options?\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<[`UseHotkeyOptions`](../interfaces/UseHotkeyOptions.md)\\> = `{}`\n\nOptions for the hotkey behavior\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Examples\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkey } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst count = ref(0)\n\n// Callback always has access to latest count value\nuseHotkey('Mod+S', (event, { hotkey }) => {\n  console.log(`Save triggered, count is ${count.value}`)\n  handleSave()\n})\n</script>\n```\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkey } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst isOpen = ref(false)\n\n// enabled option is reactive\nuseHotkey('Escape', () => {\n  isOpen.value = false\n}, { enabled: isOpen })\n</script>\n```\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkey } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst editorRef = ref<HTMLDivElement | null>(null)\n\n// Scoped to a specific element\nuseHotkey('Mod+S', () => {\n  save()\n}, { target: editorRef })\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div ref=\"editorRef\">...</div>\n</template>\n```\n"}
